  "num_options": "4",
  "section": [
    {
      "name": "Technical",
      "num_qs": 20,
      "marks": 30,
      "question": [
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "270798",
          "text": "<p>The term $\\text{Central processing unit}$ actually refers to :</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>Arithmetic and Logic unit, control unit and Memory</li>\n    <li>Memory and Control unit</li>\n    <li>Control Unit and Arithmetic and logic unit</li>\n    <li>Arithmetic and logic unit only</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-coa3",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "270796",
          "text": "The fundamental job of central processing unit is:<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  to schedule set of jobs in some order based on implementation.<br /> </li><li>  to fetch and decode sequence of instructions.<br /> </li> <li> to execute a sequence of stored instructions.<br /> </li>  <li> None of the above.  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-coa3",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "270794",
          "text": "<p>A decoder plays an important role in</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>Vertical microprogramming</li>\n    <li>Horizontal microprogramming</li>\n    <li>Multilevel microprogramming</li>\n    <li>All types of microprogramming</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-coa3",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "270792",
          "text": "<p>Consider following statements:</p>\n\n<ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type:lower-roman\">\n    <li>ROM is not used in hardwired control units.</li>\n    <li>Microprogrammed Control unit is common in CISC type systems.</li>\n    <li>Chip size if quite huge in case of Hardwired control unit than that of Microprogrammed control unit.</li>\n    <li>To modify Hardwired control unit is an easy task than doing the same with Microprogrammed control unit.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>Which of the above statements are correct?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>(ii) only.</li>\n    <li>(ii) and (iv) only.</li>\n    <li>(ii) and (iii) only.</li>\n    <li>(i) and (ii) only.</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-coa3",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "270790",
          "text": "Which of the following is not a field in control word?<br />\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>  Branch Condition bits<br /> </li><li>  Control bits<br /> </li> <li> Main memory address<br /> </li>  <li> Flag bits  </li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-coa3",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "270788",
          "text": "<p>If the control signals are generated by combinational logic then they are said to be generated by a</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>Microprogrammed control unit</li>\n    <li>Software control unit</li>\n    <li>Logic control unit</li>\n    <li>Hardwired control unit</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-coa3",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "270786",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following statements about the responsibilities of control unit is not TRUE:</p>\n\n<p>$S_1$: It causes the processor to step through a series of micro-operations in the proper sequence, based on the program being executed</p>\n\n<p>$S_2$: It generates the control signals that cause each micro-operation to be executed.</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>Only $S_1$</li>\n    <li>Only $S_2$</li>\n    <li>Both of $S_1$ and $S_2$</li>\n    <li>None</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-coa3",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "270784",
          "text": "<p>Consider following statements:<br>\n$S_1:$ Hardwired control unit requires fixed logic circuit.<br>\n$S_2:$ Vertical microprogrammed control unit requires additional combinational circuitry in order to perform certain kinds of selections.<br>\n$S_3:$ In genaral, instructions in Horizontal microprogramming control unit consume less space than instructions in vertical microprogramming.</p>\n\n<p>Which of the above statements are not correct?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$S_3$ Only</li>\n    <li>$S_1$ and $S_2$ Only</li>\n    <li>$S_1$ and $S_3$ only</li>\n    <li>All three</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-coa3",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "270782",
          "text": "<p>Consider following sequence of micro operations:<br>\n$t1: MAR \\leftarrow (PC)$<br>\n$t2: MBR \\leftarrow Memory$<br>\n$t3: PC \\leftarrow (PC) + 1; \\quad IR \\leftarrow (MBR)$</p>\n\n<p>What is the job being performed here?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>Store word</li>\n    <li>Instruction fetch cycle</li>\n    <li>Interrupt service</li>\n    <li>Context switching</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-coa3",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "270780",
          "text": "<p>Consider following statements about &nbsp;Horizontal Micro-programmed control Unit:</p>\n\n<ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type:lower-roman\">\n    <li>Horizontal Micro-programmed control Unit is thin in nature when compared to its vertical counter part.</li>\n    <li>It is faster than its vertical counterpart.</li>\n    <li>Horizontal Micro-programmed control Unit allows lower degree of parallelism than vertical counterpart.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>Which of the above statements are correct?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>(i) only.</li>\n    <li>(ii) only</li>\n    <li>(iii) only</li>\n    <li>None</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "gb2019-coa3",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "270778",
          "text": "<p>A $32$ bit system employs a micro program control unit to generate a total of $150$ control signals. Assume that during the execution of any of $100$&nbsp;micro-instructions, at least $3$ control signals and at most $5$ control signals are active. The branch address field determines the address as the branch target based on a dozen of different conditions. Minimum number of bits required in the control word, if $4$ miscellaneous bits are there, is:</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$40$</li>\n    <li>$44$</li>\n    <li>$51$</li>\n    <li>$55$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-coa3",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "270776",
          "text": "The number of clock cycles needed to perform the micro-operations required for interrupt cycle on a RISC machine, assuming PC can be modified in parallel with other micro-operations whenever possible, is______",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "3",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "gb2019-coa3,numerical-answers",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "270774",
          "text": "<p>Consider two different designs of Control unit as follows:</p>\n\n<ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type:lower-roman\">\n    <li>A part of a bigger task is improved twenty times than it was before. The other part of the same task constitutes $65\\%$ of the overall task time.</li>\n    <li>The designer can make changes to improve $72\\%$ of the task $80\\%$ faster.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>Which of the following is true about these two improvements:</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>(ii) is a better modification.</li>\n    <li>(i) is $18\\%$ faster than (ii)</li>\n    <li>(i) is $18\\%$ slower than (ii)</li>\n    <li>None of the above</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-coa3",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "270772",
          "text": "<p>Consider a CPU where all the instructions require $10$ clock cycles to complete execution. There are $205$ instructions in the instruction set. It is found that $101$ control signals are needed to be generated by the control unit. While designing the horizontal microprogrammed control unit, double address field format is used for branch control logic. What is the minimum size of the control word and a control address register?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$125, 7$</li>\n    <li>$125, 12$</li>\n    <li>$135, 9$</li>\n    <li>$135, 10$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-coa3",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "270770",
          "text": "<p>An instruction set of a processor has $266$ control signals. These signals operate in $8$ mutually exclusive groups as follows:</p>\n\n<p>$\\text{Group&nbsp;1 : 38&nbsp;signals,}$<br>\n$\\text{Group 2&nbsp;: 75&nbsp;signals,}$<br>\n$\\text{Group&nbsp;3 : 46 signals,}$<br>\n$\\text{Group&nbsp;4 : 10 signals,}$<br>\n$\\text{Group&nbsp;5 : 30 signals,}$<br>\n$\\text{Group 6&nbsp;: 18&nbsp;signals,}$<br>\n$\\text{Group 7&nbsp;: 25 signals,}$<br>\n$\\text{Group 8&nbsp;: 24&nbsp;signals,}$</p>\n\n<p>How many bits of the control words can be saved by using vertical microprogramming over horizontal microprogramming if $14$ and $33$ additional control bits are employed by horizontal microprogramming and vertical microprogramming respectively?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$43$</li>\n    <li>$186$</li>\n    <li>$190$</li>\n    <li>$204$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-coa3",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "270768",
          "text": "<p>Consider following statements:</p>\n\n<ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type:lower-roman\">\n    <li>Program execution time increases when instructions in program implement relatively higher number of microinstructions.</li>\n    <li>In a load/store architecture, the only instructions that access memory are load and store types.</li>\n    <li>More powerful instructions lead to better performance since the total number of instructions executed is smaller for a given task with more powerful instructions.</li>\n    <li>An add operation has $3$ operands ($2$ input and $1$ output), therefore add instructions must be $3$‐address instructions.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>Which of the above statement/s is/are not correct?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>(i) only</li>\n    <li>(i) and (ii) only</li>\n    <li>(i), (ii)and (iii) only</li>\n    <li>(iii) and (iv) only</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-coa3",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "270766",
          "text": "<p>Consider following micro-operations:</p>\n\n<ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type:lower-alpha\">\n    <li>ACC $\\rightarrow$ MBR</li>\n    <li>MBR $\\rightarrow$ ACC</li>\n    <li>MAR $\\rightarrow$ MBR</li>\n    <li>PC $\\rightarrow$ MAR</li>\n    <li>IR $\\rightarrow$ MAR</li>\n    <li>SP $\\rightarrow$ MAR</li>\n    <li>M[MAR] $\\rightarrow$ MBR</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>The sequence of above microoperations which are needed to perform LOAD M[LOC] instruction is:</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>(a), (d), (b)</li>\n    <li>(d), (b), (c)</li>\n    <li>(a), (c)</li>\n    <li>(e), (g)</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-coa3,datapath",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "270764",
          "text": "In a control unit the set of signals is divided into $4$ different groups as follows:\n\nGroup A with $140$ signals\nGroup B with $70$ signals\nGroup C with $230$ signals\nGroup D with $35$ signals\n\nDue to group C there is an additional overall delay of $300ns$ in the unit while every group in the control word has a delay of $4 ns$ per bit.\n\nSince group C contains a big number of signals, an improvement in this design is introduced and group C is broken down into three subgroups as:\n\nGroup P with $66$ signals\nGroup Q with $78$ signals\nGroup R with $86$ signals\n\nWith this modification the delay is modified to $5 ns$ per bit per group for all groups. The value of speed up achieved is ________",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "1.98",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "gb2019-coa3,numerical-answers",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "270762",
          "text": "<p>Consider the datapath shown below:<br>\n<img alt=\"GATEBOOK-2019-COA3-19\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p>\n\n<p>In this datapath, Instruction memory, Data Memory, Adder, Multiplexer, ALU, Registers &nbsp;and Control blocks have latencies of $400 ps \\text{(pico seconds)}, 350 ps, 100 ps, 30 ps, 120 ps, 200 ps \\text{ and } 100 ps,$ respectively.<br>\nConsider the addition of a multiplier to the ALU. This addition will add $300 ps$ to the latency of the ALU. The result will be 5\\% fewer instructions executed since we no longer need to emulate the MUL instruction.<br>\nNote that a cycle time is defined as the time needed to execute an instruction completely. For example, $\\text{Load &nbsp;word}$ loads a word from data memory to one of the data registers in one cycle.<br>\nIf $(p,q)$ denotes the values of cycle times with and without above mentioned improvement, which of the following represents correct value of $(p,q)$?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$(1130,1630)$</li>\n    <li>$(1160,1530)$</li>\n    <li>$(1430, 1730)$</li>\n    <li>$(1360,1630)$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "gb2019-coa3",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "270760",
          "text": "Consider a common control unit built using combinational logic. The operation decoder has a delay of $20 \\: ns$, Control signal geneartor has a delay of $50 \\: ns$ and the next control state generator has delay of $10 \\: ns$. A program contains 4 lines of identical type of instructions. Each line of instruction generates ten microinstructions. After executing first four microinstructions there is a jump instruction which brings the control to microinstruction $8$ after which the remaining microinstructions are executed linearly. If the jump operation consumes negligible amount of time what is the total time required to run this program in nanoseconds _________",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "1760",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "gb2019-coa3,numerical-answers",
          "category": "CO & Architecture"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}